Yes. **You can give your modified mediasoup fork a completely new proprietary brand name and present it as your own GlucoSense technology platform**, provided you continue complying with the mediasoup license.

mediasoup is currently distributed under the permissive **ISC License**. That license permits commercial use, modification, copying, and distribution, including incorporation into proprietary products. Its principal condition is that the original copyright and ISC permission notice remain with copies of the mediasoup-derived software. ([mediasoup.org][1])

The important distinction is this: **your new brand can be proprietary; your new code and enhancements can be proprietary; but you should not represent the original mediasoup code itself as having been created by GlucoSense.** The ISC license does not impose a GPL-style copyleft requirement that forces your proprietary enhancements to become open source. ([mediasoup.org][1])

